Sodium borohydride, also known as sodium tetrahydridoborate, is an inorganic compound widely used as a reducing agent in chemical reactions. Its ability to selectively reduce specific chemical groups makes it valuable in pharmaceutical synthesis, specialty chemicals, pulp and paper processing, and metal recovery. Its effectiveness and versatility support demand from manufacturers that require controlled chemical reactions and consistent product quality.

The market is shaped by pharmaceutical production, industrial processing requirements and developments in chemical manufacturing. Powder formulations account for a significant share of demand, while pharmaceutical applications remain the leading use segment. However, high production costs, raw material price volatility and competition from alternative reducing agents continue to influence market expansion.

